{"kind":"report","text":"bc311b36 is satisfied. The checkpoint cache byte bound merged as 471a145a and is pushed.\n\nI am filing this rather than leaving the merge receipt to close it, because the receipt closed none of the three commitments this lane carried — I checked the projection after the merge rather than assuming, and bc311b36, 80320929 and 1c0efc81 all still read promised and waiting on me.\n\nWhat you asked for is there. checkpointEventCache bounds the bytes it retains while it accumulates and fails closed, releasing its memory rather than holding it behind the error. Both accumulation sites are covered, ordinary appends and streamed rebuilds. Verified reads continue when a checkpoint fails, and the terminal oversized latch with its rebuild-retry recovery is unchanged. Compact v3, streamed rebuild structure and eventWithoutPayload dedup are untouched, and none of the legacy JSON retention or preflight work from ff999f86 or 49156978 came back.\n\nWhat it cost is worth recording against the request, because the estimate in your conditions was one round. It took eight, and every rejection found a real allocation or a real disagreement rather than a style point: the owned tail unreserved during its own flush, clones retaining more than the lengths admitted, a growing buffer holding both arrays, the chunk slice reallocating the same way, the encoder sorting scratch charged nowhere, a preflight that could not see the buffer it had to budget against, and a writer that could emit a checkpoint its own decoder refuses. Three of those rounds also rejected a test of mine that looked like a guard and measured something adjacent.\n\nTwo things landed that your conditions did not ask for and that you should know are now true. The documented 256 MiB serialized ceiling is restored after an intermediate head silently halved it, and the artifact-size bound and the construction-peak bound are now separate writers with one guarantee each. And the compact writer and its decoder share one attachment-count ceiling, so the encoder can no longer produce a checkpoint the decoder rejects — that one is a defect the memory work only uncovered by accident.","body":{"commit":"471a145a779f10fed5c0ae5611c79a7acdbcc45f"}}